The CPU backend times its nodes for stable-diffusion.assembly's profile

When sdasm_profile_enabled() says so -- SDASM_PROFILE is set in the environment -- the first thread of the pool times each node of a graph, from its start to the barrier after it, where the last thread is done with it, and the graph to the barrier at its end, and hands the times to sdasm_profile_node(), with the number of the graph's nodes, which tells the graphs apart, and to sdasm_profile_graph(), with the nodes themselves, as the graph holds them. stable-diffusion.assembly sums them by operation, by operands and by graph, and writes them out when the program ends (sources/profile.cc). Without the variable, a graph asks once whether to time it and times nothing.

The functions are stable-diffusion.assembly's, declared by its header, which patch 0001 includes.

This is stable-diffusion.assembly's own patch, applied to the submodule by cmake/Patches.cmake when CMake configures, after patch 0001; it is not for upstream. ggml's part is under the MIT License, and the patch's under the GNU General Public License, version 3 or any later version.

diff --git a/src/ggml-cpu/ggml-cpu.c b/src/ggml-cpu/ggml-cpu.c
--- a/src/ggml-cpu/ggml-cpu.c
+++ b/src/ggml-cpu/ggml-cpu.c
@@ -3315,6 +3315,11 @@
     GGML_PRINT_DEBUG("thread #%d compute-start cplan %p last-graph %d\n", state->ith, (const void *)cplan, state->last_graph);
 #endif
 
+    // stable-diffusion.assembly's profile: the first thread times each node
+    // to the barrier after it, and the graph to the barrier at its end.
+    const bool profiling = state->ith == 0 && sdasm_profile_enabled();
+    const uint64_t graph_start = profiling ? sdasm_profile_now() : 0;
+
     for (int node_n = 0; node_n < cgraph->n_nodes && atomic_load_explicit(&tp->abort, memory_order_relaxed) != node_n; node_n++) {
         struct ggml_tensor * node = cgraph->nodes[node_n];
 
@@ -3327,6 +3332,8 @@
             continue;
         }
 
+        const uint64_t node_start = profiling ? sdasm_profile_now() : 0;
+
         // TODO: move fused-op detection into ggml_graph_plan so fusion decisions are made once at planning time
         // Try fused ops, fall back to normal compute
         const int n_fused = ggml_cpu_try_fuse_ops(cgraph, node_n, &params, cplan);
@@ -3345,6 +3352,9 @@
         if (node_n + 1 < cgraph->n_nodes) {
             ggml_barrier(state->threadpool);
         }
+        if (profiling) {
+            sdasm_profile_node(cgraph->n_nodes, node, n_fused, sdasm_profile_now() - node_start);
+        }
     }
 
 #ifdef GGML_USE_OPENMP
@@ -3354,6 +3364,9 @@
 #endif
 
     ggml_barrier(state->threadpool);
+    if (profiling) {
+        sdasm_profile_graph(cgraph->nodes, cgraph->n_nodes, sdasm_profile_now() - graph_start);
+    }
 
 #ifdef GGML_USE_CPU_RISCV64_SPACEMIT
     ggml_backend_cpu_riscv64_spacemit_clear_numa_thread_affinity_threaded(state->ith);
